minios-installer (3.0.3) unstable; urgency=high

  * Use minios-gui 1.1.0 for the shared HeaderBar, module presentation metadata,
    and keyboard-accessible contextual Help popovers.
  * Register compact format-1 kernel package state for native installations.
  * Validate kernel payload hashes, dependencies, architecture, repository
    metadata, and pinning before publishing native bootloader state.
  * Use the native target's existing APT sources for tracked kernel packages;
    do not publish Installer-owned source entries or target keyrings.
  * Keep unverified mixed-architecture native layouts disabled, validate kernel
    symlinks, and verify ownership from one trusted dpkg list per package.
  * Install the verified dual-architecture EFI chain from the live medium.
  * Fail before manual UEFI disk changes when a reused ESP cannot use firmware
    variables, conflicts with the required GRUB vendor layout, or lacks the
    transactional free space required for safe EFI publication.
  * Preserve explicit reused-ESP identity through native EFI publication,
    including empty existing ESPs, and register MiniOS in firmware as required.
  * Verify newly created MiniOS firmware entries by label, loader, ESP identity,
    active state, and BootOrder; never delete unrelated newly observed entries.
  * Reject contradictory manual partition actions before disk mutation: delete
    is terminal for an existing partition and shrink may be staged only once.
  * Keep automatically created live and native ESPs fixed at 100 MiB and reject
    EFI payloads that would not fit before disk mutation.
  * Confirm NTFS alongside resizes non-interactively after the safety checks,
    without enabling ntfsresize force mode.
  * Make destructive-operation warnings match the actual risk: alongside resize
    explicitly acknowledges possible data loss and boot repair, manual warnings
    apply only when existing partitions are changed, and canceling does not
    imply that completed disk writes can be rolled back.
  * Keep single-language GRUB menus synchronized with the current boot-entry
    labels so localized installs do not mix translated and English entries.
  * Require the published dataclasses backport on Python 3.6 and remove the
    incomplete in-tree fallback.
  * Remove the obsolete in-tree PO update helper; translations are maintained
    through Lokit while normal PO-to-MO package builds remain unchanged.
  * Keep the README title version-neutral so release numbers cannot go stale.

