minios-installer (3.0.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Add automatic structured per-run logs with ISO timestamps, severity levels,
    installation-plan summaries, backend calls, and reproducible shell commands.
  * Keep installer log history under /var/log/minios with a latest-run symlink,
    restricted permissions, legacy-log migration, and /tmp fallback; keep logs
    on the running MiniOS system instead of copying them to the target.
  * Capture chroot command output and failures, normalize the chroot APT locale,
    summarize staged APT packages and size, and redact plaintext passwords and
    account password hashes from every logged command.
  * Stage and validate the complete native target package dependency closure
    before disk changes, including initramfs dependencies absent from the live
    system, then repair and install packages from the offline target cache.
  * Report throttled file-copy progress with transferred size, throughput, and
    elapsed time, reserving 100 percent for successful tar completion.
  * Mount /dev/pts in target chroots to support package tools without pseudo-TTY
    warnings.
  * Remove live-oriented MiniOS applications from native targets while keeping
    MiniOS Store and required system components.
  * Keep security profile identifiers as installer-only presets and let explicit
    live-config command-line settings override profile defaults.
  * Add regression coverage for logging, password redaction, package staging,
    copy completion, native cleanup, and BIOS/UEFI boot layouts.

