minios-installer (3.0.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Rework the installer into a multi-step GTK wizard with sidebar navigation,
    revisitable completed steps, partition previews, and final destructive
    confirmation.
  * Add a safe scan, plan, and execute partition pipeline bound to stable device
    identity and exact geometry.
  * Add full native installation alongside the live module layout, including
    target configuration, package preflight, initramfs, and bootloader setup.
  * Add erase-all, existing free-space, alongside, and native manual placement
    with interactive geometry controls and optional native swap.
  * Add native manual partitioning with staged create, delete, shrink, format,
    filesystem reuse, mount-point assignment, undo/reset, exact-sector previews,
    destructive confirmation, ordered multi-mount deployment, and UUID fstab.
  * Add automatic alongside installation for safe, unmounted final ext2/ext3/
    ext4 and NTFS partitions, with resize-tool detection and an explicit package
    installation action when required tools are missing.
  * Add independent firmware and partition-table selection, including UEFI on
    MBR and shared-ESP UEFI/GPT multiboot installations.
  * Add selectable MiniOS modules with required lower layers and a minios-deploy
    CLI for disk listing, plan preview, dry runs, confirmed installs, and live
    configuration overrides.
  * Add security-profile selection for live and native installs, with separate
    SSH and XRDP service controls and a --security-profile command-line option.
  * Add a Network step with hostname and wired DHCP/static IPv4 configuration.
    Native static configuration is written as a NetworkManager profile.
  * Add native, DynFileFS, raw-image, and LUKS live-session persistence modes;
    show LUKS only with runtime initrd support and verify every source initrd
    before disk changes.
  * Calculate required installation space from selected modules, boot assets,
    persistence, and proportional filesystem reserve instead of fixed defaults.
  * Generate and persist selected locales for native installations.
  * Add native cleanup of live-only packages and artifacts after native system
    configuration, generate missing OpenSSH host keys and SSL snakeoil
    certificates, and stage required native multiboot packages.
  * Write minios-configurator-compatible user, system, keyboard, service,
    network, security, and advanced live configuration.
  * Update package dependencies, compact MiniOS styling, documentation,
    translations, command-line validation, and automated tests.

